# These run on the box. CRLF would make bash reject the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The compose file is copied to the box too; a stray CR would end up inside values.
*.yml text eol=lf

# The scripture skill's script is copied into both agent workspaces and run
# there, so it needs the same shebang protection the shell scripts get.
*.py text eol=lf

# Every Markdown file, for two different reasons.
#
# Runtime, for the skill files: one is copied into both agent workspaces and its
# YAML frontmatter is parsed on the box, so a stray CR would ride along inside the
# description the model is shown. That rule used to live on its own line above and
# this one superseded it, because gitattributes takes the last match.
#
# Review, for everything else: an editor that rewrites the endings turns a
# fourteen-line change into a thirteen-hundred-line diff and buries it, which has
# happened twice on this work.
*.md text eol=lf
